The greeting is "sup"
====================

"Sup bitch?" was doing two jobs: saying hello and doing a bit. The bit was the part that aged — it is
the first thing somebody sees, and being called that before you have typed anything is a claim about
you rather than a register. It is "Sup." now. One syllable, no question mark.

The rest of the first-run line stays exactly as it was, because that part is the useful half: *"Sup —
you're new. I'm Nora. What do I call you?"* It says who is talking and asks for a name instead of
assuming one.

